.TH V7CPP 1 "August 2026" "V7 toolchain" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v7cpp \- V7 C preprocessor (host-ported)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v7cpp
[ option ] ... [ file ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I v7cpp
is the Seventh Edition Unix C preprocessor (John Reiser, 1978), run
host-side.  It handles
.BR #include ,
.BR #define ,
.BR #undef ,
conditionals (
.BR #if ,
.BR #ifdef ,
.BR #ifndef ,
.BR #else ,
.BR #endif )
and
.BR #line ,
and expands function- and object-like macros.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-P
Suppress the
.B # "line" "file"
markers it otherwise emits to preserve line numbers.
.TP
.B \-C
Pass comments through rather than removing them.
.TP
.B \-R
Allow macro recursion.
.TP
.BI \-D " name=def"
Define
.I name
as if by
.BR "#define name def" .
.TP
.BI \-U " name"
Remove any initial definition of
.IR name .
.TP
.BI \-I " dir"
Search
.I dir
for
.B #include
files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v7cc (1)
.SH BUGS
This is not a standalone user tool in the historical sense: V7 documents
the preprocessor only as a pass of
.IR cc (1),
so it has no man page of its own; this page is provided for completeness.
